<!--
    Adaptive launcher foreground.

    The flower and the mark are emitted as one path with an even-odd fill, so the mark becomes a
    hole in the flower rather than a shape drawn on top of it. That means the icon reads as the
    brand mark at every launcher size and needs no second colour layer.

    Sizing, and why it is 58dp and not bigger
    ========================================
    An adaptive icon is 108x108dp but the launcher only *guarantees* the middle 66dp, as a circle,
    and masks whatever is outside it with whatever shape the launcher chose - a circle, a squircle,
    a rounded square. Artwork that runs to the full 108dp is therefore not clipped off, it is
    clipped to the launcher's taste, and a flower whose petals are the outermost thing on the
    canvas loses its points in every one of those masks.

    This was drawn at ~76dp, which is past even the 72dp square and well past the 66dp circle, and
    the result on device was a mark with its petals sheared off by the mask.

    58dp is the flower's diameter, computed as scale 0.0465 x the 1249-unit artboard
    (1249 x 0.0465 = 58.1). That leaves 4dp of clearance on every side inside the 66dp guaranteed
    circle, so the mark survives the most aggressive mask without shrinking so far that it reads
    as a dot on a tablet launcher.

    The translation puts the artboard's centre on the canvas centre:
    translate = 54 - (624.5 x 0.0465) = 54 - 29.04 = 24.96, rounded to 25.
-->
